   "unmapped": [
    "Each of A agents has a known sensitivity s_a in (0,1]; agent a pulling arm n receives a reward drawn from Bern(s_a*mu_n), so super-arm reward is sum_a s_a*mu_{f(a)}",
    "Super-arm is an injective assignment of A agents to N arms (each agent pulls a distinct arm)",
    "Planner knows all agent sensitivities"
   ],
   "definition_quote": "The state of arm $n$ at time $t$ is a random variable $X_{t,n}\\sim$ Bern$(\\mu_n)$ ... the reward $Y_{t,a,n}$ obtained when pulling arm $n$ is a random variable that depends on both the agent $a$ who pulls it and the arm's mean: $Y_{t,a,n}\\sim \\text{Bern}(s_a\\mu_n)$. ... At each time step, the planner selects a super-arm assigning each agent to a distinct arm."
  }
