    "number": "Theorem 2",
    "quote": "Suppose we act according to the \\textsc{Min-Width} algorithm. Then $\\forall\\delta\\in(0,1)$, the cumulative regret at time $T$ is bounded by $\\mathbb{P}\\left[R_T<A(N-1)+2\\sqrt{2ANT\\ln\\left(\\frac{2NG(T,A)}{\\delta}\\right)}\\frac{\\max\\mathcal{S}}{\\min\\mathcal{S}}\\right]>1-\\delta.$"
   },
   "confidence": "medium",
   "notes": "Restated as Theorem 4 in the appendix. R_T is defined through the means but depends on the random assignments, and the bound holds with probability 1-delta. Since G(T,A)<(T+1)^A, the log term is O(A log T), and the paper states O(sqrt(T log T)) time dependence. Mapping agents to m and arms to K is a judgement call."
